BOOKS = [
# ==================== FANTASY ====================
{'name':'The Hobbit','id':1,'price':450,'author':'J. R. R. Tolkien','description':'The Hobbit follows Bilbo Baggins, a peaceful hobbit whose comfortable life changes when he joins a group of dwarves on a dangerous journey to reclaim their homeland and treasure from the dragon Smaug. Along the way, Bilbo encounters trolls, elves, goblins, giant spiders, and a mysterious ring while discovering courage, intelligence, and leadership within himself.','genre':'fantasy'},
{'name':'Harry Potter and the Philosopher Stone','id':2,'price':399,'author':'J. K. Rowling','description':'Harry Potter and the Philosopher Stone introduces Harry, an orphan who discovers that he is a wizard and begins studying at Hogwarts School of Witchcraft and Wizardry. There he makes loyal friends, learns magic, discovers secrets about his past, and becomes involved in a dangerous mystery surrounding a powerful magical object hidden within the school.','genre':'fantasy'},
{'name':'The Name of the Wind','id':3,'price':475,'author':'Patrick Rothfuss','description':'The Name of the Wind tells the story of Kvothe, a talented young man who grows from a poor and troubled childhood into a gifted musician, magician, and student. Through his own storytelling, readers discover his adventures involving education, friendship, music, magic, romance, danger, and his mysterious search for the legendary beings responsible for tragedy in his past.','genre':'fantasy'},
{'name':'A Game of Thrones','id':4,'price':550,'author':'George R. R. Martin','description':'A Game of Thrones introduces a vast fantasy world filled with powerful families, political alliances, ancient threats, and struggles for control of the Iron Throne. Multiple characters experience loyalty, betrayal, war, ambition, and personal sacrifice as events unfold across kingdoms. The story combines political intrigue with supernatural mysteries and explores the consequences of power and difficult choices.','genre':'fantasy'},
{'name':'The Lion, the Witch and the Wardrobe','id':5,'price':299,'author':'C. S. Lewis','description':'The Lion, the Witch and the Wardrobe follows four siblings who discover a magical world called Narnia through an ordinary wardrobe. Narnia is suffering under the rule of the White Witch, who has created an endless winter. The children become involved in a struggle between good and evil and learn about bravery, sacrifice, friendship, loyalty, and hope.','genre':'fantasy'},
{'name':'The Golden Compass','id':6,'price':425,'author':'Philip Pullman','description':'The Golden Compass follows Lyra, a curious young girl living in a world where humans are accompanied by animal companions called daemons. Her life changes when she becomes involved in a mysterious investigation involving missing children and powerful organizations. Her journey takes her through unfamiliar landscapes while she learns about friendship, courage, truth, authority, and the mysterious nature of her world.','genre':'fantasy'},
{'name':'The Way of Kings','id':7,'price':650,'author':'Brandon Sanderson','description':'The Way of Kings takes place in a massive fantasy world shaped by ancient conflicts, powerful storms, warriors, scholars, and mysterious supernatural forces. Several characters struggle with personal failures while becoming connected to a larger conflict. The story explores honor, leadership, responsibility, survival, friendship, and the difficult process of overcoming fear while building an expansive magical world.','genre':'fantasy'},
{'name':'Eragon','id':8,'price':350,'author':'Christopher Paolini','description':'Eragon follows a young farm boy who discovers a mysterious blue stone that eventually hatches into a dragon. His discovery changes his ordinary life and draws him into a dangerous conflict involving an evil ruler and an ancient order of dragon riders. Eragon must learn about magic, combat, responsibility, friendship, and the consequences of becoming involved in a larger war.','genre':'fantasy'},
{'name':'The Once and Future King','id':9,'price':420,'author':'T. H. White','description':'The Once and Future King retells the legendary story of King Arthur, beginning with his childhood and continuing through his rise as a powerful ruler. The story explores education, leadership, friendship, love, justice, warfare, and the responsibilities associated with power. Arthur learns important lessons from Merlin while attempting to create a fair and peaceful kingdom.','genre':'fantasy'},
{'name':'The Priory of the Orange Tree','id':10,'price':599,'author':'Samantha Shannon','description':'The Priory of the Orange Tree presents a world divided by political conflict, religious beliefs, ancient magic, and the threat of returning dragons. Different characters from kingdoms and secret organizations become connected as they prepare for a dangerous confrontation. The novel combines adventure, friendship, politics, mythology, magic, and questions about loyalty and responsibility.','genre':'fantasy'},

# ==================== MYSTERY ====================
{'name':'The Adventures of Sherlock Holmes','id':11,'price':360,'author':'Arthur Conan Doyle','description':'The Adventures of Sherlock Holmes is a collection of detective stories featuring Sherlock Holmes and Dr. John Watson as they investigate unusual crimes and mysteries. Holmes relies on careful observation, logical reasoning, evidence, and deduction to solve difficult cases. Each story presents a different puzzle involving deception, hidden motives, suspicious characters, and unexpected discoveries.','genre':'mystery'},
{'name':'Murder on the Orient Express','id':12,'price':399,'author':'Agatha Christie','description':'Murder on the Orient Express follows detective Hercule Poirot as he investigates a murder that occurs aboard a luxurious train during a journey across Europe. The train becomes trapped by heavy snow, leaving the passengers isolated while Poirot questions everyone and examines the evidence. The mystery gradually reveals complicated relationships, hidden identities, motives, and surprising connections.','genre':'mystery'},
{'name':'The Murder of Roger Ackroyd','id':13,'price':375,'author':'Agatha Christie','description':'The Murder of Roger Ackroyd centers around the mysterious death of wealthy businessman Roger Ackroyd in a quiet English village. Hercule Poirot becomes involved in the investigation and carefully examines the statements and actions of everyone connected to the victim. The case contains secrets, misleading evidence, suspicious relationships, and one of detective fiction’s most memorable revelations.','genre':'mystery'},
{'name':'The Hound of the Baskervilles','id':14,'price':425,'author':'Arthur Conan Doyle','description':'The Hound of the Baskervilles follows Sherlock Holmes and Dr. Watson as they investigate a mysterious curse affecting the Baskerville family. A terrifying legend claims that a supernatural hound has hunted members of the family for generations. Holmes approaches the case logically while strange events occur around an isolated estate, creating a suspenseful mystery involving fear, deception, and murder.','genre':'mystery'},
{'name':'The Girl with the Dragon Tattoo','id':15,'price':499,'author':'Stieg Larsson','description':'The Girl with the Dragon Tattoo follows journalist Mikael Blomkvist and highly skilled investigator Lisbeth Salander as they investigate the decades-old disappearance of a wealthy businessman’s niece. Their investigation uncovers disturbing family secrets, financial crimes, violence, and hidden relationships. The story combines investigative journalism, technology, suspense, complex characters, and a gradually intensifying search for the truth.','genre':'mystery'},
{'name':'The Big Sleep','id':16,'price':350,'author':'Raymond Chandler','description':'The Big Sleep follows private detective Philip Marlowe as he becomes involved in a complicated case concerning a wealthy family and its troubled members. What initially appears to be a simple investigation quickly becomes filled with blackmail, deception, murder, and competing motives. Marlowe must navigate dangerous situations while trying to determine which characters are telling the truth.','genre':'mystery'},
{'name':'The Maltese Falcon','id':17,'price':390,'author':'Dashiell Hammett','description':'The Maltese Falcon follows private detective Sam Spade as he becomes involved in a dangerous search for a valuable and mysterious statue. Several criminals and wealthy individuals pursue the object while attempting to manipulate one another. Spade must deal with deception, betrayal, murder, and shifting alliances while trying to understand who can be trusted and what everyone truly wants.','genre':'mystery'},
{'name':'Rebecca','id':18,'price':410,'author':'Daphne du Maurier','description':'Rebecca follows a young woman who marries a wealthy widower and moves into his impressive estate. There she constantly feels overshadowed by his deceased first wife, Rebecca, whose presence seems to remain everywhere. As the new wife learns more about the household and its secrets, she begins questioning what really happened in the past and whom she can trust.','genre':'mystery'},
{'name':'The Woman in White','id':19,'price':450,'author':'Wilkie Collins','description':'The Woman in White begins when a young drawing teacher encounters a mysterious woman dressed entirely in white on a lonely road. Her strange appearance becomes connected to an unusual family and a complicated inheritance. As the story develops, characters uncover secrets involving identity, deception, marriage, money, and manipulation while attempting to understand the truth behind the mysterious woman.','genre':'mystery'},
{'name':'And Then There Were None','id':20,'price':380,'author':'Agatha Christie','description':'And Then There Were None brings ten strangers to an isolated island after each receives an invitation from an unknown host. One by one, the guests begin dying under mysterious circumstances while a terrifying sense of suspicion spreads throughout the group. With no obvious escape and everyone appearing suspicious, the remaining characters desperately try to discover who is responsible.','genre':'mystery'},

# ==================== ROMANCE ====================
{'name':'Pride and Prejudice','id':21,'price':280,'author':'Jane Austen','description':'Pride and Prejudice follows Elizabeth Bennet, an intelligent young woman who initially dislikes the wealthy and seemingly arrogant Mr. Darcy. As their relationship develops, both characters discover that their first impressions were incomplete. The novel explores love, marriage, family expectations, social class, personal growth, pride, misunderstanding, and the importance of looking beyond appearances when judging another person.','genre':'romance'},
{'name':'Jane Eyre','id':22,'price':330,'author':'Charlotte Bronte','description':'Jane Eyre follows an independent young woman who experiences hardship from childhood before becoming a governess at Thornfield Hall. There she develops a complicated relationship with the mysterious Edward Rochester. Jane struggles between love, personal independence, morality, and social expectations while discovering secrets about Rochester and his household. The novel emphasizes dignity, emotional strength, equality, and personal identity.','genre':'romance'},
{'name':'Wuthering Heights','id':23,'price':310,'author':'Emily Bronte','description':'Wuthering Heights tells the passionate and troubled story of Heathcliff and Catherine Earnshaw, whose relationship is shaped by love, social expectations, resentment, and revenge. Their decisions affect multiple generations of families living around the Yorkshire moors. The novel explores intense emotions, obsession, social class, grief, revenge, and the destructive consequences of refusing to let go of past relationships.','genre':'romance'},
{'name':'Sense and Sensibility','id':24,'price':295,'author':'Jane Austen','description':'Sense and Sensibility follows sisters Elinor and Marianne Dashwood, who have very different personalities and approaches to love. Elinor is practical and controlled, while Marianne expresses her emotions openly and passionately. Their experiences with relationships, disappointment, family pressure, and social expectations teach them important lessons about emotional balance, maturity, trust, and understanding other people.','genre':'romance'},
{'name':'Little Women','id':25,'price':340,'author':'Louisa May Alcott','description':'Little Women follows the four March sisters as they grow up during a period when their father is away at war. Meg, Jo, Beth, and Amy have different personalities, ambitions, and dreams, but remain closely connected through family affection. The story explores sisterhood, friendship, love, personal growth, creativity, sacrifice, responsibility, and the challenges of becoming an adult.','genre':'romance'},
{'name':'The Notebook','id':26,'price':299,'author':'Nicholas Sparks','description':'The Notebook tells the story of Noah and Allie, two young people who fall deeply in love despite differences in their social backgrounds and family expectations. Years later, their relationship is remembered through an older man reading from a notebook. The story explores lasting love, memory, separation, forgiveness, commitment, aging, and the emotional power of relationships that survive difficult circumstances.','genre':'romance'},
{'name':'Me Before You','id':27,'price':370,'author':'Jojo Moyes','description':'Me Before You follows Louisa Clark, a cheerful young woman who becomes a caregiver for Will Traynor, a wealthy man whose life changed after an accident. Their initially difficult relationship gradually develops into a meaningful connection. Through their experiences, both characters reconsider their ideas about happiness, independence, love, possibility, and what it means to live a fulfilling life.','genre':'romance'},
{'name':'The Fault in Our Stars','id':28,'price':330,'author':'John Green','description':'The Fault in Our Stars follows Hazel Grace Lancaster and Augustus Waters, two teenagers who meet through a support group and develop a close relationship. Their friendship grows through conversations, humor, shared experiences, and an unusual literary connection. The story explores love, family, friendship, mortality, hope, dreams, and the importance of finding meaning in limited and uncertain circumstances.','genre':'romance'},
{'name':'The Time Traveler’s Wife','id':29,'price':425,'author':'Audrey Niffenegger','description':'The Time Traveler’s Wife follows Henry, a man who involuntarily travels through different moments of his life, and Clare, the woman who loves him despite the unusual circumstances. Their relationship develops across different points in time, creating challenges involving uncertainty, separation, marriage, family, and memory. The novel explores whether love can remain strong despite circumstances beyond human control.','genre':'romance'},
{'name':'One Day','id':30,'price':350,'author':'David Nicholls','description':'One Day follows Emma Morley and Dexter Mayhew, two people who meet after graduating from university and remain connected for many years. The story revisits their lives on the same date across different stages, showing how friendship, career, relationships, mistakes, and personal growth shape their connection. It explores timing, love, regret, ambition, friendship, and changing priorities.','genre':'romance'},

# ==================== SCIENCE FICTION ====================
{'name':'Dune','id':31,'price':499,'author':'Frank Herbert','description':'Dune takes place on the desert planet Arrakis, the only known source of a valuable substance that is essential to interstellar civilization. Paul Atreides becomes involved in a dangerous political conflict after his family is given control of the planet. The story combines politics, ecology, religion, warfare, prophecy, family loyalty, and the struggle for control over valuable resources.','genre':'science fiction'},
{'name':'The Martian','id':32,'price':480,'author':'Andy Weir','description':'The Martian follows astronaut Mark Watney after he is accidentally left behind on Mars and presumed dead by his crew. Alone on a hostile planet, he must use scientific knowledge, engineering, creativity, and careful planning to survive. Meanwhile, scientists on Earth attempt to develop a way to rescue him. The story emphasizes problem solving, persistence, teamwork, and human ingenuity.','genre':'science fiction'},
{'name':'Project Hail Mary','id':33,'price':550,'author':'Andy Weir','description':'Project Hail Mary follows a scientist who awakens aboard a spacecraft with no memory of how he arrived there or why he has been sent into space. As his memories gradually return, he discovers that humanity faces a major threat. He must use scientific reasoning, experimentation, and cooperation to understand the problem and find a solution capable of saving humanity.','genre':'science fiction'},
{'name':'Ender’s Game','id':34,'price':390,'author':'Orson Scott Card','description':'Ender’s Game follows Ender Wiggin, a highly intelligent child selected to attend a military training program designed to prepare young people for a possible conflict with an alien species. Through increasingly difficult simulations and challenges, Ender learns strategy, leadership, teamwork, and empathy. The story also raises questions about manipulation, responsibility, childhood, war, and the morality of using children in conflict.','genre':'science fiction'},
{'name':'Foundation','id':35,'price':425,'author':'Isaac Asimov','description':'Foundation explores the decline of a vast galactic empire and the efforts of mathematician Hari Seldon to reduce the chaos expected to follow its collapse. Seldon develops a new field that attempts to predict large-scale social behavior. The story examines politics, science, leadership, civilization, historical patterns, knowledge, and the challenges of preserving human progress during periods of enormous change.','genre':'science fiction'},
{'name':'Fahrenheit 451','id':36,'price':320,'author':'Ray Bradbury','description':'Fahrenheit 451 presents a future society where books are forbidden and firefighters are responsible for destroying them rather than preventing fires. Guy Montag is a firefighter who begins questioning his role after meeting people who think differently from society. The novel explores censorship, independent thought, technology, conformity, knowledge, entertainment, and the importance of protecting ideas and intellectual freedom.','genre':'science fiction'},
{'name':'The War of the Worlds','id':37,'price':350,'author':'H. G. Wells','description':'The War of the Worlds describes an invasion of Earth by technologically advanced beings from Mars. Human society struggles to respond as the invaders demonstrate powerful weapons and seemingly unstoppable machines. Through the experience of ordinary people caught in the invasion, the story explores survival, fear, scientific progress, human vulnerability, social order, and the consequences of encountering a civilization more technologically advanced than our own.','genre':'science fiction'},
{'name':'Do Androids Dream of Electric Sheep?','id':38,'price':375,'author':'Philip K. Dick','description':'Do Androids Dream of Electric Sheep? takes place in a future world damaged by environmental destruction and nuclear conflict. Bounty hunter Rick Deckard is assigned to locate and retire advanced androids that have escaped to Earth. As he investigates, he begins questioning what separates humans from machines. The story explores identity, empathy, artificial intelligence, morality, technology, and human consciousness.','genre':'science fiction'},
{'name':'Neuromancer','id':39,'price':450,'author':'William Gibson','description':'Neuromancer follows Case, a skilled computer hacker whose career has collapsed after he is punished for stealing from an employer. He receives an opportunity to return to cyberspace by joining a dangerous mission organized by mysterious figures. The novel explores artificial intelligence, hacking, corporations, technology, identity, virtual reality, and the relationship between human consciousness and machines.','genre':'science fiction'},
{'name':'The Left Hand of Darkness','id':40,'price':410,'author':'Ursula K. Le Guin','description':'The Left Hand of Darkness follows an envoy sent to the distant planet Gethen to encourage its people to join a larger interplanetary civilization. The planet has unusual social and biological characteristics that challenge the envoy’s assumptions about gender and society. The story explores culture, identity, politics, friendship, isolation, trust, and the difficulty of understanding people from completely different societies.','genre':'science fiction'},

# ==================== HISTORICAL FICTION ====================
{'name':'The Book Thief','id':41,'price':390,'author':'Markus Zusak','description':'The Book Thief follows Liesel Meminger, a young girl growing up in Nazi Germany during the Second World War. She finds comfort in books and begins stealing them while forming relationships with people around her. Her family also hides a Jewish man in their home. The story explores friendship, courage, loss, kindness, war, family, and the power of words.','genre':'historical fiction'},
{'name':'All the Light We Cannot See','id':42,'price':475,'author':'Anthony Doerr','description':'All the Light We Cannot See follows Marie-Laure, a blind French girl, and Werner, a German boy with a talent for radio technology, during the Second World War. Their lives develop separately before eventually intersecting during the conflict. The novel explores war, survival, courage, science, family, morality, communication, and the choices ordinary people make during extraordinary historical events.','genre':'historical fiction'},
{'name':'The Nightingale','id':43,'price':450,'author':'Kristin Hannah','description':'The Nightingale follows two sisters living in France during the Second World War as they respond differently to the German occupation. One becomes involved in resistance activities while the other struggles to protect her family under difficult circumstances. Their experiences reveal the courage, sacrifice, fear, and resilience of women and families living through wartime occupation and uncertainty.','genre':'historical fiction'},
{'name':'A Thousand Splendid Suns','id':44,'price':420,'author':'Khaled Hosseini','description':'A Thousand Splendid Suns follows two Afghan women, Mariam and Laila, whose lives become connected through difficult circumstances during decades of political and social upheaval. Despite hardship, violence, and restrictive conditions, they develop a powerful friendship and protect one another. The novel explores family, sacrifice, friendship, resilience, motherhood, survival, and the effects of historical conflict on ordinary people.','genre':'historical fiction'},
{'name':'The Kite Runner','id':45,'price':399,'author':'Khaled Hosseini','description':'The Kite Runner follows Amir, a boy growing up in Afghanistan who develops a close friendship with Hassan. A traumatic event changes their relationship and leaves Amir carrying guilt for many years. As Afghanistan experiences major historical changes, Amir eventually returns to confront his past. The story explores friendship, betrayal, guilt, redemption, family, courage, and forgiveness.','genre':'historical fiction'},
{'name':'The Pillars of the Earth','id':46,'price':575,'author':'Ken Follett','description':'The Pillars of the Earth is set in medieval England and follows several characters whose lives become connected through the construction of a magnificent cathedral. Builders, nobles, clergy, and ordinary people become involved in political conflicts, personal rivalries, ambition, and social struggles. The novel presents medieval society while exploring architecture, power, religion, love, betrayal, and perseverance.','genre':'historical fiction'},
{'name':'The Help','id':47,'price':380,'author':'Kathryn Stockett','description':'The Help is set in Mississippi during the 1960s and follows three women from very different backgrounds whose lives become connected through domestic work and writing. Two Black women working as maids and a young white aspiring writer begin sharing their experiences despite social pressures. The story explores friendship, discrimination, courage, social expectations, dignity, and the desire for change.','genre':'historical fiction'},
{'name':'The Tattooist of Auschwitz','id':48,'price':425,'author':'Heather Morris','description':'The Tattooist of Auschwitz is based on the experiences of a Jewish prisoner during the Second World War who is forced to tattoo identification numbers onto other prisoners. Despite living under horrific conditions, he forms a relationship with another prisoner and attempts to protect her and others whenever possible. The story explores survival, courage, love, hope, and human resilience.','genre':'historical fiction'},
{'name':'The Guernsey Literary and Potato Peel Pie Society','id':49,'price':360,'author':'Mary Ann Shaffer and Annie Barrows','description':'The Guernsey Literary and Potato Peel Pie Society follows writer Juliet Ashton as she begins corresponding with residents of the island of Guernsey after the Second World War. Their letters reveal stories about life under German occupation and the unusual literary society they created. The novel explores friendship, community, books, courage, humor, loss, and the healing effects of storytelling.','genre':'historical fiction'},
{'name':'The Alice Network','id':50,'price':440,'author':'Kate Quinn','description':'The Alice Network connects the stories of two women from different generations whose lives are shaped by war and espionage. One woman worked as a spy during the First World War, while another searches for a missing person after the Second World War. Their partnership uncovers secrets from the past while exploring courage, friendship, betrayal, trauma, sacrifice, and redemption.','genre':'historical fiction'}
]